# xWN10-AU-000580: Audit MPSSVC Rule‑Level Policy Change Failures

> **Warning!** Audit Deprecated  
> This audit is deprecated and will be removed in a future update.

## Information  
Maintaining a robust audit trail is essential for identifying configuration errors, troubleshooting service disruptions, and detecting potential compromises.  
The **MPSSVC** service (Microsoft Protection Service) enforces firewall and IPSec rules. Auditing rule‑level policy changes ensures that any unauthorized or unexpected modifications to MPSSVC policies are logged.

## Solution  
Enable failure auditing for MPSSVC rule‑level policy changes by configuring the corresponding advanced audit policy.

### Policy Path  
```text
Computer Configuration
└─ Windows Settings
   └─ Security Settings
      └─ Advanced Audit Policy Configuration
         └─ System Audit Policies
            └─ Policy Change
               └─ “Audit MPSSVC Rule‑Level Policy Change”


Desired Setting
Failure (log only failed attempts)
Step‑by‑Step Remediation

Open Group Policy Editor
Press Win + R, type gpedit.msc, and press Enter.
Navigate to Advanced Audit Policies
In the left pane expand:


Computer Configuration
└─ Windows Settings
   └─ Security Settings
      └─ Advanced Audit Policy Configuration
         └─ System Audit Policies
            └─ Policy Change

Locate “Audit MPSSVC Rule‑Level Policy Change”
In the Policy Change folder, find Audit MPSSVC Rule‑Level Policy Change.
Enable Failure Auditing
Double‑click the setting.
Check Failure (uncheck Success if selected).
Click OK.
Refresh Policy Settings
Open an elevated Command Prompt and run:

gpupdate /force

Verify Audit Configuration
Open an elevated PowerShell prompt and run:

auditpol /get /subcategory:"MPSSVC Rule‑Level Policy Change"

Ensure Failure is listed under “Audit Policy” for this subcategory.


